d change when the stock of  the bank started to drop in late 2007.  you see sean thought that this was just  a great biotic opportunity  and that it was just a matter of time  until the bank recovered so sean doubled  down on his bet and it took out loans  against other companies to buy contract  for differences or cfds cfds are a type  of financial derivative and its inner  workings are quite complex but all you  need to know is that it's a form of  leveraged trading this means the gains  and losses in share price are amplified  for example if the share price recovers  2 you might make 20  but the problem is that if it drops 2  percent you lose 20  now there's no excuse for borrowing  money to make such a gamble but sean  wasn't an idiot either there were a  couple of big misleading green flags  that led him down this path first of all  anglo-stock was performing way better  than the rest of the banking industry  this doesn't mean that english stock was  at all-time highs but it was down less  than the overall financial industry this  made sean confident that other investors  also saw the potential in anglo but the  reality was that a dozen extremely well  the individuals were propping up the  share price  once anglo stock started to fall anglo  allegedly reached out to its top 10  biggest investors and directors and gave  them loans to buy anglo stock apparently  this is why shawn himself was buying  anglo stock so all this extra buying  pressure created a false sense of  security aside from popping up the stock  price anglo was allegedly propping up  their fundamentals anglo had loaned out  money to one of their rivals who then  turned around and deposited the money  back into anglo which made it seem like  anglo was more solvent than they really  were this charade helped anglo stay  afloat through the beginning of the  financial crisis but as other financial  institutions started to collapse angler  would collapse as well  and sean was basically all in on anglo  got obliterated  given that sean had lost it all on anglo  stock he was no longer able to pay back  his loans to anglo and anglo would come  after sean shawn and his family have  fired back with lawsuits against anglo  claiming that they basically propped up  the stock price and fundamentals it was  never really determined if these  allegations were true or not but here's  what we know  anglo did in fact give out a loan to top  investors directors and a rival who in  turn invested back into anglo but anglo  claims that there were no laws being  broken they were simply fulfilling their  roles as a bank by loaning out money and  giving out financial advice it's not  like they were committing securities  fraud or running a pump and dump also it  wasn't the bank's fault that sean went  all in on anglo stock he was clearly  smart enough in the 1990s to diversify  away from construction he should have  known not to put all his eggs in one  basket regardless of how confident he  was in the investment with not enough  money left to run his businesses sean  would voluntarily file for bankruptcy in  northern ireland but even this would end  poorly you see sean's choice to file  from bankruptcy in northern ireland was  strategic because the law in northern  ireland allows bankrupt businesses to  return to business after 12 months  however a judge would overturn this  bankruptcy filing asserting that sean's  main businesses were run out of ireland  and not just northern ireland this made  it impossible for sean to restart his  business without paying back his loans  but without his businesses there was no  chance that he could ever pay them back  so sean was stuck in a catch-22  situation this went on until ireland  decided to nationalize anglo-irish bank  and bail them out with 34 billion euros  once the bank was nationalized it wasn't  just a bank who wanted chant to repay  his loans now it was the state and they  were looking to take away all his  remaining assets seeing this sean and  his kids would try to weigh as many  assets as they could offshore but they  would quickly be caught and charged  resulting in sean being sent to joe for  nine weeks and with that sean had  officially fallen from being islands  which is men to being a convict  all these lawsuits and court battles  have been extremely expensive for both  sean and the state apparently the battle  cost the state a total of 170 million  euros as of 2019 so they finally decided  to settle the case the court has agreed  to let the queen family keep 440 million  euros if they liquidate their remaining  assets and pay back at least 500 million  euros to the state so it looks like the  quinn family will end up walking away  with a large sum of money nonetheless  this has left a lot of the public  divided a lot of people in ireland still  strongly support sean suggesting that  sean made a calculated risk on anglo and  if it wasn't for anglo's deception  sean's investment would have panned out  they feel that ireland unfairly took  sides with anglo and that shawn is  innocent on the other side of spectrum  critics argued that it doesn't matter  whether anglo was deceptive or not  sean's leveraged investment was  extremely irresponsible and he's simply  facing the consequences of his actions  not to mention it it was the people who  trusted sean and brought his insurance  policies that sustained the most  impactful losses in the meantime it  looks like sean is still walking away  with 440 million euros critics also  point to shawn's instinct to hide away's  assets as a glimpse at his true colors  at the end of the day shawn started off  as a poor farm boy who used his  ingenuity and humbleness to reach  unthinkable heights at one point he was  cherished by the irish and regarded as a  miraculous success story but it only  took one overconfident investment to  destroy the empire and reputation that  he had so painstakingly built who do you  think is to blame sean or anglo comment  t